 "history": "NEA was founded in 1977 by Dick Kramlich, Chuck Newhall and Frank Bonsal, with a $16 million first fund and offices on both coasts. Among its first bets was 3Com, which brought Ethernet to market, and later it backed Salesforce, Workday, Uber, Robinhood and Databricks. In 2023 it closed about $6.2 billion across two funds, its largest raise, and it manages about $35 billion from Menlo Park, New York and London.",
